<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:16:10Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Iran poised to exploit security vacuum as US leaves Iraq</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d60d582d38714bafe1e56d8b6282cd212aa8605eb5c7543d0dd83142176861ac</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-poised-to-exploit-security-vacuum-as-us-leaves-iraq/a-79550833--9d1cbb2d4ce5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-poised-to-exploit-security-vacuum-as-us-leaves-iraq/a-79550833?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The end of the US military mission in Iraq leaves the Kurdistan region facing a severe security vacuum. As Erbil grapples with deep internal divisions, Tehran is well positioned to make strategic gains.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What China's new military foothold in Laos means for Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0276fe1572966910935b742fae4ec4ef393cd4771b89ecd931c8323131085ac</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-china-s-new-military-foothold-in-laos-means-for-southeast-asia/a-79548259--642cd34d5dd0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-china-s-new-military-foothold-in-laos-means-for-southeast-asia/a-79548259?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Beijing says its new Laos facility will train pilots. Analysts see a broader signal: China's growing military presence in mainland Southeast Asia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Suspected pneumonic plague in Siberia: What we know about the disease</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7a33b1a5ef29546b64f8c7a2e2088cab2ff335a8866a111188d698366d17089</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T11:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919--6c7e74a1d6ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A worker at a plague research institute in Siberia has died, and nearly 200 of her contacts are under medical observation. Russian authorities deny a link to the bacterial infection. The US is monitoring the situation.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia election: New steps to prevent electoral fraud, but nationalist parties remain on top</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5cd2569406e699c845f698392308a585460c2c22efcf7572f0e72f8a73cd8a36</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-election-new-steps-to-prevent-electoral-fraud-but-nationalist-parties-remain-on-top/a-79544717--5102b97990e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-election-new-steps-to-prevent-electoral-fraud-but-nationalist-parties-remain-on-top/a-79544717?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New technology has stopped votes being cast on behalf of dead or absent voters, and turnout has fallen to a record low. But it was a case of deja vu in Bosnia's elections with the same parties winning.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's mental health crisis in the wake of Oct. 7 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60bd8fb9a055e0a2fdbf930571ef85245e8b05b0561a1e571c170e935fa4c1e7</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:15:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T08:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-s-mental-health-crisis-in-the-wake-of-oct-7-attacks/a-79507122--40bc5ac1f942.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-s-mental-health-crisis-in-the-wake-of-oct-7-attacks/a-79507122?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than a third of Israelis have shown symptoms of mental health conditions, a report found. Three years after the October 7 attack, the country's health system is still struggling to come to terms with its effects.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hundreds of French schools shut, teen loses hand in protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27c76859db7d335a22347245755ae75327fa28e0eb0e50c008e7cc117b9ec909</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:16:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T05:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hundreds-of-french-schools-shut-teen-loses-hand-in-protests/a-79542656--d9ec9cc932b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hundreds-of-french-schools-shut-teen-loses-hand-in-protests/a-79542656?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The student protests that rocked France last week have prompted authorities to keep up to 500 schools closed on Monday. A teenage boy lost his hand, seemingly while trying to pick up a police tear gas grenade.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil election: Bolsonaro and Lula head to runoff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9cf6cc9ff2cae4bbf6621d0209797b9c2c660d797a9e26bac9065beb53cb6e83</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T00:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-election-bolsonaro-and-lula-head-to-runoff/a-79533857--ed3bf9e023d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-election-bolsonaro-and-lula-head-to-runoff/a-79533857?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Populist Flavio Bolsonaro has secured a thin lead over incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, but the next president of Brazil will be decided in the runoff round, according to the country’s electoral court.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nationalists top Bosnia-Herzegovina's divisive election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d0f40d1d48fd1b1230203f8d7d7275df9cb0ee4e4efebb0793a55f7ca150964</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T22:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nationalists-top-bosnia-herzegovina-s-divisive-election/a-79535336--ff55c4d27908.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nationalists-top-bosnia-herzegovina-s-divisive-election/a-79535336?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bosnia-Herzegovina's three-member presidency is set to be dominated by nationalists from the three major ethnic groups, including Zeljka ​Cvijanovic, backed by disqualified Serb secessionist leader Milorad Dodik.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>In Tigray, Ethiopian government forces have advanced against a northern rebel group, reports indicate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e707a0b5c893478bdec615f59c95e66d5883235ed3e7abaa5716c053af44def3</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T03:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-tigray-ethiopian-government-forces-have-advanced-against-a-northern-rebel-group-reports-indicate/a-79534372--ed90e271ae47.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-tigray-ethiopian-government-forces-have-advanced-against-a-northern-rebel-group-reports-indicate/a-79534372?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Reports indicate Ethiopian government forces have made advances against a northern rebel group. Renewed fighting has raised fears the conflict could spill over into the wider region.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Peru: Fire burning on road to Machu Picchu kills 1</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a752c78d154bfced1ff02d856f5ad3111afb28bb5801ae63af8abaafd6e7820e</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T02:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/peru-fire-burning-on-road-to-machu-picchu-kills-1/a-79534344--e801992ff38b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/peru-fire-burning-on-road-to-machu-picchu-kills-1/a-79534344?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One person has died and two others have suffered burns in a fire near the main access route to the historic sanctuary of Machu Picchu.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>AI giants 'not being nearly careful enough,' warns outgoing OpenAI safety engineer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1628a82b5949dd4f195b0fed2aa8d69ea1361533a269131e7e53531973c4fa93</id><updated>2026-10-05T17:14:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T21:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-giants-not-being-nearly-careful-enough-warns-outgoing-openai-safety-engineer/a-79533080--b451aed5afe0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-giants-not-being-nearly-careful-enough-warns-outgoing-openai-safety-engineer/a-79533080?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Days after US President Donald Trump signed a voluntary pact with artificial intelligence giants, a former OpenAI worker said his industry needs the same safeguards as nuclear power or aviation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan vs. Afghanistan: From allies and neighbors to war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c75b1d4095ed6bf1ca1cd5c5